            // ...
            validation + loop_overhead + dead_check + polygon_push + queue_update
        ).count();
```

and the broad timing window here:

```711:818:simplify.cpp
while (cur < int(stream.size())) {
    auto loop_start = Clock::now();
    // ... almost the whole iteration ...
    g_timing.loop_overhead += Clock::now() - loop_start;
}
```

So the right interpretation is: `loop_overhead` means “un-instrumented work inside the loop,” not “loop machinery.”

